  "articleBody": "Installing custom trim can really elevate a room, but it's easy to stumble if you're not careful. One of the biggest pitfalls is poor measurement. You've heard it a million times: measure twice, cut once! This is especially true with trim, where even a tiny miscalculation can lead to visible gaps or wasted materials. Make sure to check your dimensions room by room, and don’t assume all walls are perfectly square. Another common mistake is incomplete surface preparation. If your walls aren't clean, smooth, and dry, your trim won't adhere properly, leading to an unprofessional finish. Take the time to clean and sand surfaces before you start. Using the wrong tools for the material is another pitfall; different types of trim – wood, MDF, PVC – require specific blades, adhesives, and fasteners for the best results. And finally, failing to account for corners, joints, or finish details can make even well-cut pieces look bad. Careful alignment, pre-drilling when necessary, and meticulous caulking and painting are crucial for that polished look. When in doubt, a professional like Abraham and his team at HH Remodeling LLC can handle these details, ensuring a beautiful and lasting installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
